Child of tracker 0266 (pillage manifest,
docs/pillage-0266-agentic-reproduction-2026-07-12.md, technique 5); serves
tracker 0236 (trace-doctor) — listed there as a child.

## Context

trace-stats.py classifies turns with a binary nav/work discriminator
(_is_nav_tool, from 0243 H11) plus a raw tool counter. The paper's six-way
taxonomy — execution, reading, navigation, search, writing, other — with
per-category character volume (arXiv:2604.21965 §5.2, App. B.2) surfaced
real per-scaffold behavioral findings; the same cut would sharpen the
trace-doctor census.

## Actions

1. Extend the classifier to a six-way category function over tool name +
   input.
2. Track per-category call count and char volume (extend the existing
   byte tracking).
3. Add per-category report columns, joinable by skill/entry point.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Six-way classifier implemented, pure Python, unit-tested
- [ ] Report includes per-category count + char volume
- [ ] 0236 tracker body lists this child
